{"title":"2012 CEMC Galois Problems/Problem 2a","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2012 CEMC Galois Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_2a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>When the numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are taken in pairs and averaged, what are the three averages?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_2a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, the possible pairs are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/2/ba2b54aa0a8d81a9f8fac3925a87556b25d61fa6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(25, 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"51\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/d/7fd77ebd8392eb6efcaa3707af09afd4deef1b1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(25, 29)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"60\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/a/08ac4050cb03031d5677411ccf060b043eb8e511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5, 9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p>Each pair has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers. Thus, we will divide the sum of each pair by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> when calculating the average.\n</p><p>The sum of the numbers in the first pair is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/3/93390ba9aadc66761dd96049b60f503e2f56b609.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25 + 5 = 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />. This means that its average is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/0/b90a6d97130657ff135843aafe9f33a56be7eb5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{30}{2} = \\boxed{15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"78\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>The sum of the numbers in the second pair is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/5/b9554a94445c3d92c38ddf75fd27fcaabda668c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25 + 29 = 54$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" />. This means that its average is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/f/11fdb4df18153627c1df0f710130d1496d7ed0d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{54}{2} = \\boxed{27}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"78\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>The sum of the numbers in the third pair is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/6/216b57cb8cf3a6cb1f578c46640f1171d65b773c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 + 9 = 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" />. This means that its average is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/8/8882ab3a52d67bbed3251aa237867da402c6a41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{14}{2} = \\boxed{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"69\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017230544\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.011 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.015 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 58/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 78/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2518/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.872      1 2012_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_2\n100.00%    5.872      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:35642:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017230544 and revision id 278094. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}